{"event": "token", "client_ms": 21731, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:13.165Z", "t_ms": 21678, "delta": "### §1: Motivation\nLarge language models struggle with basic tasks such as accessing"}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 21982, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:13.417Z", "t_ms": 21929, "delta": " up-to-date information, avoiding factual hallucinations, understanding low-resource languages, performing precise arithmetic calculations, and tracking the"}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 22356, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:13.735Z", "t_ms": 22248, "delta": " progression of time [C2]. Existing approaches address this by providing access to external tools, but they typically depend on extensive human annotations or are"}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 22663, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:14.004Z", "t_ms": 22516, "delta": " restricted to task-specific settings [C2]. Toolformer aims to overcome these limitations by teaching language models general-purpose tool use in a"}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 22838, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:14.273Z", "t_ms": 22785, "delta": " self-supervised way, enabling the model to autonomously choose when and how to invoke tools without large-scale human supervision [C3].\n\n###"}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 23175, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:14.503Z", "t_ms": 23016, "delta": " §2: Approach\n* **Tool Representation:** Tools are accessed via API calls whose inputs and outputs are represented as text sequences delimited"}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 23483, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 40, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:14.860Z", "t_ms": 23372, "delta": " by special tokens (e.g., `<API>`, `</API>`, and `->`) [C4].\n* **Sampling Candidate Calls"}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 23664, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 41, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:15.095Z", "t_ms": 23607, "delta": ":** Starting with an ordinary text dataset, the model is prompted with a handful of human demonstrations for each API [C3]["}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 23880, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 42, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:15.315Z", "t_ms": 23828, "delta": "C5]. The model computes the probability of starting an API call at different positions and samples candidate calls where the probability exceeds a threshold ["}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 24111, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 43, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:15.545Z", "t_ms": 24058, "delta": "C5]. \n* **Execution & Filtering:** The candidate API calls are executed to obtain their text responses [C5]."}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 24507, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 44, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:15.845Z", "t_ms": 24358, "delta": " Calls are retained only if providing both the call and its result reduces the weighted cross-entropy loss over subsequent tokens by at least a threshold"}}
{"event": "token", "client_ms": 24742, "data": {"request_id": "1231a1fdc918", "seq": 45, "ts": "2026-10-27T17:39:16.175Z", "t_ms": 24688, "delta": " $\\tau_f$ compared to the best alternative of either making no call or making the call without its response [C"}}
